<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<StyleSet xmlns="http://adamantium/ui"
          xmlns:x="http://adamantium/ui/xaml/extensions">

    <!-- Plain text. Nothing here differs from Fluent's numbers - macOS's metrics do not override FontSizeBody, so both
         themes resolve the same key - and the file exists anyway, because this theme answers for every control ITSELF
         rather than borrowing. "The same as the other theme, and here is where you change it" is an answer; a missing
         file is a question.

         Worth knowing what a setter here means now: a selector that narrows by nothing but the type is filed as a
         DEFAULT for that type (ValuePriority.TypeDefault), below inheritance - so this dresses loose text and steps
         aside inside a control, where the control's own state colour reaches its content. Before that slot existed a
         style in this file would have silently stopped every selected row and pressed button in the application from
         following its state, which is why the file used to be empty in every theme. See TypeDefaultSlotTests. -->

    <Style Selector="TextBlock">
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ObservableResource TextFillColorPrimary}"/>
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{ResourceReference FontSizeBody}"/>
    </Style>

</StyleSet>
